    "summary": "This PR attempts to harden the custom-rules engine against ReDoS by capping regex pattern length at 1,000 chars, allowlisting regex flags to gimsuy, stripping/ deduping flags at execution time, capping inline `code` at 500,000 chars, and limiting `path` file size to 500,000 bytes. It touches `src/core/customRulesEngine.ts`, `src/server/handlers.ts`, `src/server/inputParser.ts`, plus docs/tests. Reviewers should verify whether the chosen mitigations actually address catastrophic-backtracking ReDoS, since pattern/input length caps do not bound exponential regex execution.",
    "risk_level": "high",
    "rule_findings": [],
    "suggestions": [
      {
        "file_path": "src/core/customRulesEngine.ts",
        "line": 138,
        "severity": "high",
        "confidence": 0.72,
        "title": "Length caps do not mitigate ReDoS (catastrophic backtracking)",
        "reason": "The PR's stated goal is to prevent ReDoS, but the added guard `if (pattern.pattern.length > MAX_PATTERN_LENGTH)` (and the companion `MAX_CODE_LENGTH` / `MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES` caps) only bound input/pattern *size*, not regex execution time. ReDoS is caused by exponential backtracking in short patterns, so the new limits leave the vulnerability exploitable. A pattern far under 1,000 characters still hangs the process.",
        "recommendation": "Complement the size caps with an actual ReDoS mitigation: run regex matching in a worker/child process with a hard timeout, or use a linear-time engine such as `re2` (e.g. `new RE2(pattern.pattern, safeFlags)`), or statically reject nested quantifiers / back-references before compiling. Keep the length caps as secondary defenses but do not rely on them to close the ReDoS issue.",
        "source": "ai",
        "evidence": [
          "      if (pattern.pattern.length > MAX_PATTERN_LENGTH) {"
        ],
        "failure_scenario": "A client calls `add_custom_rule` with a 6-character pattern `(a+)+$` (passes `ALLOWED_FLAGS_RE`, well under 1,000 chars), then calls `execute_custom_rules` with `code` = 'a'.repeat(40) + '!' (under 500,000 chars). Both guards pass, the global regex undergoes catastrophic backtracking, and the server blocks until timeout/OOM instead of returning issues."
      }
    ],
